WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:01.934
- Today is Saturday, huh?

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:02.767
- [Mark] You what?

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.935
- Today is Saturday, right?

00:00:03.935 --> 00:00:04.957
- [Mark] Today's Saturday, yeah.

00:00:04.957 --> 00:00:08.874
- I didn't realize today
was Saturday the 15th.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.633
I think this is the first time

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:13.133
I've seen you down here on a Saturday.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.583
- [Mark] It's a Saturday.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.340
All right, so, Jerry.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.173
- [Jerry] Yes.

00:00:22.173 --> 00:00:23.410
- [Mark] So, we had a
whole bunch of setbacks

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.490
with your apartment.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.150
The painting, and the
getting it furnished,

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.270
and new clothes, and all that.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:33.270
We had COVID, we had the
rioting that happened downtown.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.710
Then, Gary in your
building, who worked there,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.400
passed away from COVID.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.233
- Yeah.

00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.641
It's been nothing, but-

00:00:39.641 --> 00:00:41.450
So, all the GoFundMe
money that we generated

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.960
for you has just been sitting there.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.540
I've been paying your
rent, which is great,

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.920
but that's pretty much
all we were able to do

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:49.763
for a long time.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.290
But, you got new clothes you got new bed,

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.430
towels, kitchen stuff, new apartment.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.263
All painted up.

00:00:57.263 --> 00:00:58.480
Everything's all nice and new.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.970
- [Jerry] Yes, I appreciate
that, Mark, very much.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.570
- [Mark] So, what's the nicest thing about

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.403
having an apartment rather than

00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:03.690
living on the street, as you were?

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.653
When I first met you.

00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:07.820
- [Jerry] Well, you get a lot of rest,

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:10.592
you clean yourself up,

00:01:11.681 --> 00:01:12.527
and

00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:16.190
you stay warm in the
winter time. It's great!

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.023
It's really good.

00:01:17.023 --> 00:01:18.230
- [Mark] A place to hang out.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.030
- On the streets, I
was getting sick a lot.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.018
- [Mark] You would get sick a lot?

00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:24.601
- On the streets, yeah.
If it's cold, yeah.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.310
I feel more safer.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.143
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:35.071
- Being on the streets,
you're not really asleep.

00:01:35.071 --> 00:01:37.780
You might get a time where
you you're not really asleep,

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.790
because you never know who's around.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.063
You know, people walking around all over.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.440
It's great to be inside.
It's all thanks to you, Mark.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.573
Yes, definitely. Yeah.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:50.613
- [Mark] Well, you've become like a

00:01:50.613 --> 00:01:52.014
mini celebrity now because of your video.

00:01:52.014 --> 00:01:53.042
- Yes, a lot of people.

00:01:53.042 --> 00:01:54.290
- [Mark] People recognize you.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.410
- Yeah, people, yeah. I've
seen your video, yeah.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.390
- [Mark] Do people come up
to you all the time and-

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.420
- Yeah, they tell me about it. Yeah

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.460
- [Mark] Say nice things
to you, rather than-

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.251
- Yeah, they mention your name too.

00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:06.073
And they know I'm inside
this place here too.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:07.830
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.660
- They know I'll be inside
this place, taking a video.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.020
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.073
- Yeah, 'cause they seen it before.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.810
They ask, "Where's that place you was in?"

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.450
I say, "That's our Studio."

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.465
Yeah, they asked about it.

00:02:21.465 --> 00:02:23.810
They asked about this.
Yeah. You been inside. Yeah.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.643
Yeah.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:26.010
- [Mark] Well, it's nice that
people now know your story.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:26.843
- Yep, yep.

00:02:26.843 --> 00:02:28.000
- [Mark] Because I think
a lot of people were

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.390
just frightened by you or whatever.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.310
- Right, right. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.450
- [Mark] Now they know the
backstory and it's like-

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.510
- A lot of people come to me.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.720
I didn't know about you, about, you know,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.707
what happened or anything like that.

00:02:40.707 --> 00:02:41.540
They think I'm-

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.030
They treat me sometimes like
I'm being on the streets,

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.253
Yeah.

00:02:46.253 --> 00:02:47.960
- [Mark] So, I've come to
see you many, many times now.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.930
Probably a hundred times I've come over

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.000
and your mood is so consistent.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.470
Every single time I see you,

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.760
you're in a great mood,
just as you are now.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.510
You're personable, you're pleasant.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.320
And you never get down from your situation

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.520
or what happened to you?

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.803
- [Jerry] Don't worry
about things in life.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.900
You know where I get that from?

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.810
- [Mark] Where's that?

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.043
- [Jerry] That's in the Bible.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.480
It says don't worry about things in life.

00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:23.610
And you say, "How come?".

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.370
I say,

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.137
"I can't change this."

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.474
I can go into a shell if I want to.

00:03:33.474 --> 00:03:36.505
I can really go in a shell.

00:03:36.505 --> 00:03:37.338
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:37.338 --> 00:03:40.650
Use it as an excuse, but I can't do that.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.243
- [Mark] Do you ever feel like a victim?

00:03:43.311 --> 00:03:44.810
- [Jerry] No, not really.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.560
- [Mark] So many people
I talk to are always

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.740
are telling these victim stories.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.875
They're victims, they're victims.

00:03:49.875 --> 00:03:50.708
- [Jerry] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:50.708 --> 00:03:51.673
- [Mark] And I never hear that from you.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.093
- [Jerry] A lot of people
know what happened to me.

00:03:56.093 --> 00:03:58.200
They know more about me than I do.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.597
There's rumors out there that

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.383
I broke into a house
while people was there.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.072
And shot me in my face.

00:04:10.072 --> 00:04:11.520
(Jerry laughs)

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.798
I always hear stories down here.

00:04:12.798 --> 00:04:15.123
Everybody knows things about me.

00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:18.090
More than I do.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:22.070
But like I said,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.370
I gotta keep moving on.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.473
I can't let this bring me way down.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:30.868
And thank God.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.530
I'd lose my mind.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.753
A lot of people probably
couldn't take this.

00:04:42.591 --> 00:04:44.027
A lot of guys out there,

00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:47.932
they don't like me.

00:04:47.932 --> 00:04:49.903
For one thing, Mark, is this here,

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.360
They seen this, right here.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.670
I don't know nothin'.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.123
And then,

00:04:59.714 --> 00:05:00.547
they talk to me and find out

00:05:00.547 --> 00:05:02.880
I'm not what they thought I was.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.713
Damn you.

00:05:05.168 --> 00:05:06.978
They say, "Damn you!"

00:05:06.978 --> 00:05:09.630
They're mad. They thought
I'd be like this here.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:10.833
I was born like this,

00:05:13.602 --> 00:05:15.393
I don't know nothin',
I'm dumb or whatever.

00:05:15.393 --> 00:05:16.863
I'm out on the streets.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.610
And then, when they get talking to me,

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.376
or anything like that,

00:05:21.376 --> 00:05:22.367
and I say, "Yes."

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.200
They don't like that.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.680
- [Mark] Right. My
favorite thing about you,

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.861
is you seem to carry no anger.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.694
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:29.694 --> 00:05:31.350
- [Mark] You don't seem
like an angry person at all.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.183
- And they get mad.

00:05:32.183 --> 00:05:34.210
- [Mark] Do you? Or about the
person that did this to you?

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.534
I mean, I think your views on forgiveness

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.460
are similar to mine.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.000
In that,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.360
you forgive for your,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.350
you're doing it for yourself.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.470
Not for the other person.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.303
- Right.

00:05:44.303 --> 00:05:45.800
- [Mark] By forgiving the other person,

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.443
you're more at peace.

00:05:49.443 --> 00:05:50.512
- I can't live life like that.

00:05:50.512 --> 00:05:55.512
I've got to keep on livin', Mark.

00:05:55.805 --> 00:05:57.313
I'd go in a shell.

00:05:58.923 --> 00:06:00.800
I can't do that though.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.643
I love life.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.814
Life is great, man.

00:06:07.814 --> 00:06:08.753
Definitely.

00:06:08.753 --> 00:06:11.190
- [Mark] I think your positive attitude-

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:12.070
- Yes, definitely.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.170
- [Mark] Is like a motivational

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.513
speech, just in itself.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.910
So, I mean, were you as
positive a person before

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.860
you're shooting?
- Yeah, definitely, yeah.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:24.693
- [Mark] You were always positive?

00:06:24.693 --> 00:06:25.573
- Yes.

00:06:25.573 --> 00:06:26.406
- [Mark] Even when you were a younger man?

00:06:26.406 --> 00:06:27.739
- I love livin'.

00:06:28.761 --> 00:06:33.440
I love livin'.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.043
I couldn't wait for morning time to come.

00:06:35.043 --> 00:06:36.843
I would get up early in the morning.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.580
And see the morning light.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.970
- [Mark] And you had a lot of friends?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:41.803
- Not too many.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.330
I like to be by myself a lot,

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:48.950
sometimes, most of the time, yeah.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.923
- [Mark] You're by yourself a lot now.

00:06:49.923 --> 00:06:51.214
- Yeah, right now.

00:06:51.214 --> 00:06:52.147
Like in that room there,

00:06:52.147 --> 00:06:56.352
I sit back and listen to
that radio you bought me.

00:06:56.352 --> 00:06:57.185
Yeah.

00:06:58.643 --> 00:06:59.806
I don't do a whole lot.

00:06:59.806 --> 00:07:03.403
I just sit in that room,
day in and day out.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.930
Nothin'.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.780
And then, plus, I got sick and stuff.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.603
I can't go out.

00:07:10.603 --> 00:07:15.130
I left my thing on the
thing too, at the house.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:16.703
That spray thing, Mark.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.740
I gotta have that with me.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.950
- [Mark] For your, you
have a problem breathing.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.760
- Yeah, I left it at my place, too.

00:07:28.143 --> 00:07:29.043
Like, for example,

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.650
say that I didn't have
any more of the stuff.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.390
I couldn't come outside for two weeks.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.313
